Package: mm-pve-tools
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 ${perl:Depends},
 pve-manager (>= 9.0),
 pve-file-restore-ntfs3g (>= 2.0)
Description: MasterMind tool modules for the Proxmox VE GUI
 Extensible toolset from MasterMind TI that lives inside the Proxmox VE
 web GUI and survives PVE package updates.
 .
 Current modules:
  * renumber - change the VMID of a VM without copying data (move_disk);
  * restore - publish a folder from a PBS backup to the customer VM over
    read-only SMB for a limited time, through a dedicated gateway VM;
  * branding - logo, favicon, title and header texts on every node.
 .
 Desired state is kept cluster-wide in /etc/pve/mm-tools/ and applied on
 each node by "mm-pve apply" (on demand, timer, boot and dpkg triggers).

Package: mm-gw-restore
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 python3,
 iproute2,
 proxmox-backup-client,
 ntfs-3g,
 ntfs-3g-plugin-dedup,
 fuse3,
 samba,
 nftables,
 iputils-arping,
 qemu-guest-agent
Description: MasterMind restore gateway for Proxmox VE backups
 Runs inside the dedicated Debian gateway VM used by the "restore" module
 of mm-pve-tools. Maps PBS backups read-only (ntfs-3g + dedup plugin) and
 publishes a single chosen folder per session through Samba with
 per-session credentials, nftables rules and VLAN isolation.
 .
 Controlled from the PVE node via the QEMU guest agent; no listening
 management port.
